<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mali Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mali empires</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mali Empire was a West African empire founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sundiata-keita">Sundiata Keita</a> around 1235, which flourished until the fifteenth century. It controlled trans-Saharan trade in gold and salt and reached its height under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mansa-musa">Mansa Musa</a>, whose pilgrimage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a> in 1324 became famous. It succeeded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana-empire">Ghana Empire</a>, and its decline was followed by the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mali-empire.jpg" alt="Mali Empire" width="320" height="225" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: HetmanTheResearcher · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_the_Mali_Empire.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
